holy:IonicCompressor50 dcterms:references <https://www.linde-engineering.com/en/images/DS_IC%2050_tcm19-523715.pdf>;
                       a owl:NamedIndividual,
                         holy:HydrogenStorage;
                       rdfs:label "Ionic Compressor 50"@en;
                       skos:altLabel "IC family"@en,
                                     "IC model"@en;
                       skos:definition "Linde's ground-breaking ionic compression technology leads the way to the next generation of safe, fast and efficient hydrogen fuelling. The ionic compressor 50 is a high-performance, easy-to-maintain solution with a listed design. It allows for quick, safe, highly efficient and economical fuelling of hydrogen vehicles at 25MPa and 35 MPa. This is achieved by an innovative compression system, the ionic compressor, where, instead of a mechanical piston, a column of ionic fluid is in direct contact with the gaseous hydrogen. This allows for the continuous high-performance, fast fuelling of hydrogen vehicles. It is designed to fuel 25-MPa and 35-MPa vehicles with the highest filling levels while considerably reducing operating costs. It is used for gaseous hydrogen."@en.
